<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        If your company uses Parties, Insights counts the parties booked at the location alongside the games. Only
        bookings still marked as booked count. Cancelled parties are left out, and provisional bookings brought in from
        Just Step Online are counted.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="The party figures">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Parties</strong>: parties starting in the range, counted on the day they start.</li>
            <li><strong>Party children</strong>: the children expected at those parties, as booked. It's the number on the
                booking, not a head count on the day.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>Games</strong>: how many games were played at parties and how many by walk-ins.</li>
            <li>In <strong>Typical week</strong>, <strong>Shade by</strong> also offers <strong>Party games</strong> and
                <strong>Party children</strong> (children on site in that hour, on average).</li>
            <li><strong>Games per day</strong> shows walk-in and party games as separate lines.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            Insights shows counts only: no child's name, contact details, allergies or prices. <strong>Export CSV</strong>
            adds four columns at the end: Walk-in games, Party games, Parties on and Expected children.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="How a game is matched to a party">
        <FluentText>
            Kiosks don't record which party played a game, so Insights works it out from the time. A game counts as a
            party's if it starts between 10 minutes before and 40 minutes after the party's laser tag time.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li>If the booking has no laser tag time, the location's <strong>Laser tag (minutes after arrival)</strong>
                in <a href="/manage/parties/settings">Party settings</a> is used. Bookings imported from Just Step Online
                never have their own laser tag time, so set this default.</li>
            <li>A laser tag private hire counts every game during the booking.</li>
            <li>A play-only private hire doesn't play laser tag, so none of its games count.</li>
            <li>A party with no laser tag time and no default counts as walk-ins. Insights says how many there were.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote>
            It's a best guess, so treat the split as approximate. Walk-ins who play inside a party's window are counted
            as the party's. A party starting laser tag more than half an hour late, or playing a third game, has those
            games counted as walk-ins. The default also applies to parties that don't play laser tag, and a venue with
            two arenas counts both arenas' games.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Parties and the staffing flags">
        <FluentText>
            A party brings its own games and its own party staff, so it would make a normal hour look busy or quiet.
            Hours with a party on are left out of the typical games per staff hour and aren't flagged. An hour that has
            a party in at least half of the weeks shows as <strong>● Mostly parties</strong> instead, and is listed
            under <strong>Hours to look at</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
